# Every set-apart quotation in this repo — a `> *"…` blockquote — and whose words
# it is. Held by `quote-check.mjs`; see that file for why this is a list and not
# a pattern (three mechanical rules were tried and each flagged tens of files of
# honest prose).
#
# A quotation of the OWNER is not declarable and never becomes declarable. Write
# what was wrong and what it measured — never who reported it, never in what
# words. Five sentences of ordinary speech survived every other gate in these two
# repos before this existed.
#
#   file | document | product-copy | analysis | the quotation's opening words
#
#   document     — a canonical text: the doctrine, a law, an ADR, a research entry
#   product-copy — an app's own strings, or a tagline
#   analysis     — a previous session's own writing, quoted to argue with or correct
#
LESSONS.md | analysis | what he is describing wants a lens — a filter you switch on
LESSONS.md | analysis | Binding constraint if a lens is built: law 1 does not bend f
LESSONS.md | analysis | Still owed, and it is your call rather than a build
